@page "/narrative-motion"

<PageTitle>Narrative motion · FancyBlazor</PageTitle>

<section class="demo-page narrative-motion-page">
    <p class="kicker">NARRATIVE MOTION / IN FLOW</p>
    <h1>Let the scroll carry the story.</h1>
    <p class="lede">These effects move with an ordinary document section. They do not pin, trap, or take over the reader’s scroll.</p>

    <ScrollBackdrop CssClass="narrative-stage" Palette="FancyPalettes.Viridian" Intensity=".42" data-testid="scroll-backdrop-example">
        <ScrollScene Effect="ScrollSceneEffect.Lift" Strength=".42" Travel="72" data-testid="scroll-scene-example">
            <article class="narrative-copy">
                <p class="specimen-label">SCENE / LIFT</p>
                <h2>Content stays in the document flow.</h2>
                <p>As this section crosses the viewport, its treatment follows local progress while its heading, text, and link remain ordinary semantic HTML.</p>
                <a class="primary-action" href="/background">See a backdrop at rest</a>
            </article>
        </ScrollScene>
    </ScrollBackdrop>

    <ScrollIndicator Color="#a7f3d0" CssClass="narrative-reading" data-testid="scroll-indicator-example">
        <article>
            <p class="specimen-label">LOCAL READING PROGRESS</p>
            <h2>ScrollIndicator</h2>
            <p>The fine line below this short chapter fills as the chapter moves through the viewport. It is decorative, so it never changes the reading order or accessibility tree.</p>
        </article>
    </ScrollIndicator>

    <section class="surface-recipe" aria-labelledby="narrative-recipe-heading">
        <div class="surface-recipe__copy">
            <p class="specimen-label">COMPOSITION / THREE COMPONENTS</p>
            <h2 id="narrative-recipe-heading">A scroll scene without scroll-jacking.</h2>
            <p>The live specimen uses a scroll-reactive background behind a continuous in-flow scene. Add an indicator when local progress helps frame a chapter.</p>
        </div>
        <pre class="surface-recipe__code"><code>&lt;ScrollBackdrop CssClass="narrative-stage" Palette="FancyPalettes.Viridian" Intensity=".42" data-testid="scroll-backdrop-example"&gt;
    &lt;ScrollScene Effect="ScrollSceneEffect.Lift" Strength=".42" Travel="72" data-testid="scroll-scene-example"&gt;
        &lt;article class="narrative-copy"&gt;
            &lt;p class="specimen-label"&gt;SCENE / LIFT&lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;h2&gt;Content stays in the document flow.&lt;/h2&gt;
            &lt;p&gt;As this section crosses the viewport, its treatment follows local progress while its heading, text, and link remain ordinary semantic HTML.&lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;a class="primary-action" href="/background"&gt;See a backdrop at rest&lt;/a&gt;
        &lt;/article&gt;
    &lt;/ScrollScene&gt;
&lt;/ScrollBackdrop&gt;

&lt;ScrollIndicator Color="#a7f3d0" CssClass="narrative-reading" data-testid="scroll-indicator-example"&gt;
    &lt;article&gt;
        &lt;p class="specimen-label"&gt;LOCAL READING PROGRESS&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;h2&gt;ScrollIndicator&lt;/h2&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;The fine line below this short chapter fills as the chapter moves through the viewport. It is decorative, so it never changes the reading order or accessibility tree.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/article&gt;
&lt;/ScrollIndicator&gt;</code></pre>
    </section>
</section>
